# pots v1.4 — a user-reported symptom during the standing phase.
#
# pots:SymptomEventShape has one Violation constraint, pots:symptom, carrying
# sh:datatype xsd:string, sh:minCount 1, sh:maxCount 1 AND sh:minLength 1. The
# last of those is the one worth noticing: a symptom event whose symptom is the
# empty string satisfies every other part and still says nothing. That case is
# symptomevent-empty-symptom.INVALID.ttl.
#
# Lightheadedness on standing is the cardinal POTS symptom and the reason someone
# runs this check at all, so it is the realistic value rather than an arbitrary
# in-range string.
#
# pots:notes is Info-severity with sh:maxLength 100. The note here is 51
# characters and the longest note this batch writes -- the one in
# potscheck-nasalean-full.VALID.ttl -- is 55, so the limit has ample margin.
# Both figures are len() of the literal, counted rather than estimated; an
# editor lengthening a note should recount rather than trust the number here.
#
# The limit is not exercised by a negative fixture because Info findings are
# invisible to this runner in both directions -- extract_violations() reads
# sh:Violation and extract_warnings() reads sh:Warning, and nothing reads
# sh:Info. Of pots:SymptomEventShape's four constraints, two are Info and
# therefore unobservable here; that is a property of the runner, not a gap in
# this fixture.
#
# Fully synthetic: not a real person's report.

@prefix pots: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/pots/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:b0750006-0000-4a00-8000-000000003010> a pots:SymptomEvent ;
    pots:symptom "lightheadedness" ;
    pots:notes "Onset at four minutes upright; resolved on sitting." ;
    pots:timestampSeconds "240.0"^^xsd:double .
